  "body": "**Adversarial audit (card `supplier-boundary-audit`, scope refined), with no \u03ba, certificate, supplier or frontier change.** Josie Elliston (JosieElliston), with Claude Code (Claude Opus 5.5) assistance, in a donated session.\n\nBase `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`; selected record SHA-256 `10b9e340\u2026`. Chooser nonce `5f419d173f49750373ab915c29fb04d7`, priority revision 3. Branch `research/t16-audit-coverage-s28`, head `6e66ea56`. Claim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18926402\n\n## Question\n\nThe selected record's only post-#1042 stage, `research/complex-t16-rare-pattern-exchanges/verify.py`, runs the frozen PR1087 `code/audit_allcold.py` (SHA-256 `1467a2ac\u2026`) through `verify_t16.py`, with 15 mutation controls. Which of the audit's acceptance predicates do those controls actually reach? For each predicate they miss, is a targeted semantic mutant rejected?\n\n## Package `research/t16-audit-mutant-coverage/`\n\n`verify.py` is stdlib only and takes about 70 s. The fixture is the selected hosted template archived in `research/community-frontier1094-audit/selected-replay.tar.gz`, so no cold run is needed. The pinned audit runs unchanged and in-process. The harness executes the shipped control block verbatim, with only `def reject` renamed, and records the `audit_allcold.py` line that rejects each mutant.\n\n| Mutant set | Count | Rejected | Accepted | Further lines with an `assert` reached first |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Shipped controls | 15 | 15 | 0 | 8 of 42 |\n| New targeted semantic mutants | 35 | 34 | 1 | 20 |\n| One-field template census | 111 | 92 | 19 | 6 |\n\n- **Positive control.** The in-process audit reproduces every field of the archived selected `ASYNC-AUDIT.json` except the two mutation-run fields.\n- **Shipped controls are concentrated.** Four of the 15 are rejected first by line 94 (the whole provider-registry equality). Three are rejected by line 152 and three by line 159.\n- **First exercised here.** Each of these is rejected at the intended assertion:\n  - the idle window from both sides (line 156);\n  - the wrong side of the idle pair, and a helper past the child's rank (line 156);\n  - overlapping axis cells across calls (line 163);\n  - a gap in the pending prefix (line 178);\n  - schedule list order and retiming (lines 114, 121, 122 and 129);\n  - pooled-slot count, key and field binding (lines 169 to 173).\n- **Accepted: 19 path mutations.**\n  - Pooled-slot `time`: line 172 omits it, so the audit alone accepts changed times.\n  - 15 fields `audit()` never reads, such as `cover`, `m`, `version`, `port_restriction`, `replica_lift`, `hosting.owner_map_sha256` and `hosting.rule`. A text search of the PR1087 archive and the maintainer frontier1094 scripts finds no reader of these in the hosted template after `emit`.\n  - Three partial checks: appended text in `loop_order` (only one sentence is required), and an extra key in `hosting` or in `async_schedule`.\n- **A cross-stage link that no selected stage checks.** The audit checks the hosted template, while `lift16`, `independent-t16` and the maintainer composition (PR1091 auditor) check the frozen `data/OWNERS.json.gz`. The verifier checks that the template's `pooled_slots` is exactly that owner list: 69,120 roles, with `time` fields included. It also checks that `owner_map_sha256` names the list's gzip. Both hold.\n- **Unreachable by template-only mutation.** Eight of the 42 lines with an `assert` cannot be reached this way, each for a stated reason. Three depend only on base inputs, and five are implied by earlier assertions or by construction.\n\n**Outcome:** no missing implication was found for the selected fixture. This is line coverage: a line with a compound condition, such as 94, 152 or 156, does not get one mutant per conjunct. The audit alone would accept changed pooled times. The fixture-level owner binding is a separate check in `verify.py`.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `python3 -B research/t16-audit-mutant-coverage/verify.py`: `EXPECTED.json` is byte-identical on CPython 3.10.21, 3.12.14 and 3.14.7 (macOS arm64).\n- `python3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/t16-audit-mutant-coverage`, both the check and the replay, passes.\n- The 42 research unit tests pass.\n- An independent read-only Codex review found no outcome-changing discrepancy in the shipped-control wrapper, the line attribution, the new mutants or the eight unreachable-line claims. Its must-fix (line totals) and two should-fixes (narrower \"no reader\" wording, separating the fixture binding from what `audit()` implies) are applied.\n\n**Not checked:**\n- mutations of base inputs (DATA-PHASES, providers, parent);\n- the module-level provider checks;\n- the invoice, assembly and indep16 stages;\n- the #1042 ancestry;\n- Linux or Windows;\n- a cold `make frontier1094-verify`.\n\n## Open next questions\n\n1. The same receipt for the nine other `audit_allcold.py` hashes in the repository (PR1939's handoff).\n2. A successor driver binding template `pooled_slots` to `OWNERS.json.gz`. This needs a maintainer decision, because the frozen code stays unchanged.\n3. Mutation testing for `invoice_allcold.py`, which carries the prefix and row inequalities and has no mutation-control block of its own.\n\n## Credit\n\n- Audited checker: the PR1087 archive's `code/`, byte-identical to Jeremy Kothe's #870 code. Its docstring credits OpenAI Codex, and it includes the T16 edits from Hao Yan's (@FanPUYen) #858.\n- Selected exchanges and run: Rohan Arun's #1094, with the run archived by the maintainer's frontier1094 audit.\n- Copy-cost observation: jackmgaller's PR1939. The harness copies by `marshal`, following it.\n- Interpreter stability of the stage: session 26's PR1824.\n- Independent OWNERS recount: PR1091.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
